{# ── Chapter: FE Depth ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="fe-depth">
  <h2>The promise has to actually be true</h2>
  <div class="tone-junior">
    <p>
      Only mark a package <code>sideEffects: false</code> if it's actually true. If the bundler removes code that secretly did matter, because a file was wrongly marked safe, you get a silent runtime bug, not a build error.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-mid">
    <p>
      Global CSS imports are the most common accidental violation: a component file that does <code>import './styles.css'</code> has a real side effect (injecting styles), and needs to be excluded from the sideEffects-false list even if the rest of the package is genuinely pure.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-staff">
    <p>
      Verify tree shaking actually happened with a real bundle analyzer, not just by trusting the config, a <code>sideEffects: false</code> field that's present but ineffective (because the bundler's minifier ran before dead-code elimination, or the import is dynamic) gives you false confidence with zero size benefit.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

